<main id="main"><section class="pageHero compact"><div class="container"><span class="kicker">Legal</span><h1>Cancellation & Refund Policy</h1><p>How service cancellation and refund requests are handled.</p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container legalProse"><h2>Before payment</h2><p>VPN4U confirms availability and the final configuration before requesting payment. If we cannot supply the requested service, no payment should be required for that unavailable order.</p><h2>VPS and VPN services</h2><p>Where consumer law gives you a statutory cancellation right, that right applies. If you expressly ask us to begin a digital service immediately, your statutory rights may be affected once performance begins. Outside mandatory rights, refunds for activated VPS or VPN periods are assessed case by case and are not guaranteed after resources have been provisioned.</p><h2>Dedicated servers</h2><p>Dedicated servers reserve physical capacity and may incur upstream setup or allocation costs. Setup charges and completed provisioning are generally non-refundable except where required by law or where VPN4U is unable to deliver the accepted service.</p><h2>Renewals</h2><p>Customers should request cancellation before the next renewal or invoice date stated in their order or billing communication. Cancellation normally stops future renewal; it does not automatically refund an already delivered service period.</p><h2>Service failure</h2><p>If VPN4U materially fails to provide an accepted service, contact <a href="mailto:<%= site.emails.support %>"><%= site.emails.support %></a>. Depending on the circumstances, we may provide repair, replacement capacity, service credit or a refund where appropriate.</p></div></section></main>
